              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a route, then the Telugu for to set foot in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: రిజర్వేషను",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రిజర్వేషను — rijarvēṣanu — \"a reservation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పండుగ రోజుల్లో రైలులో రిజర్వేషను దొరకడం కష్టం. paṇḍuga rōjullō railulō rijarvēṣanu dorakaḍaṁ kaṣṭaṁ. In the festival season it is hard to get a reservation on the train."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Like most English loans in Telugu it ends in -ఉ: రిజర్వేషను (rijarvēṣanu). It goes with చేయు: రిజర్వేషను (rijarvēṣanu) చేయించాను, I had a seat reserved."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రిజర్వేషను (rijarvēṣanu) is a loan from English reservation, a seat kept for one passenger. Telugu adds its usual -ఉ to the final consonant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
